\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Every complete accounting transaction must contain equal debit and credit amounts. A journal voucher can have two or more lines, but the combined debit must equal the combined credit.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Normal increases: Assets and Expenses increase with a Debit. Liabilities, Capital/Equity, and Income increase with a Credit. The opposite side normally records a decrease.}
