\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
3. Command Dashboard}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The Command Dashboard provides access to Chart of Accounts, Journal Entries, Ledger, Trial Balance, Income Statement, Balance Sheet, and Petty Cash. The dashboard also shows From and To dates, a Refresh control, Bank/Cash/Petty Cash summaries, Generate Monthly Total, Post Summary to Journal, and a Financial Preview area.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Use the reporting period controls before reviewing period-based information. Investigate unexpected balances through the relevant ledger rather than entering an artificial correcting entry.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
4. Chart of Accounts}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The Chart of Accounts screen lists Account ID, Account Name, Category, and Type. The Add / Edit Account area contains Account ID, Account Name, Category, Type, Add New, Update Selected, Delete Selected, and Clear.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Create accounts before using them in journal entries. Give each account a unique ID and meaningful name, then classify the Category and Type consistently. Incorrect classification can leave a journal mathematically balanced while causing the financial reports to be misleading.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Review existing combinations carefully. For example, the supplied screen shows an account named Opening Balance with Category Current Assets and Type Expense, and a Bike account with Category Other Expense and Type Assets. Confirm that such combinations match the intended accounting treatment before relying on reports.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
5. Journal Entries and Vouchers}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The New Journal Line section contains Date, Voucher No., Account, Description, Debit, Credit, Add Line, and Start New Voucher. The screen also displays Journal out-of-balance total, which should return to 0.00 when the voucher is complete.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
To record a voucher, enter all debit and credit lines that belong to one transaction. Use the same voucher number for the related lines. After the voucher balances, start the next voucher using the application workflow.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The journal history area displays Date, Voucher Number, Account ID, Account, Description, Debit, and Credit, with From, To, Account, Apply, and Clear filters. The supplied screen shows matching overall Total Debit and Total Credit of 10,787,218.85 and Closing Balance 0.00.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Delete Selected Line should be used cautiously. Removing only one side of a completed voucher can leave the accounting record unbalanced. After any correction, recheck the voucher, ledger, and trial balance.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
6. Ledger}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The Ledger groups journal postings by account so users can review debit movements, credit movements, and resulting balances. Use the Ledger to investigate unusual cash, bank, petty cash, income, expense, liability, or capital balances.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
A journal presents transactions by voucher/date; a ledger presents the accumulated activity of an individual account. If a report looks incorrect, the relevant ledger is one of the first places to investigate.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
7. Trial Balance}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The Trial Balance summarizes ledger balances into Debit and Credit columns. As a fundamental control, total debits should equal total credits.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
An equal Trial Balance does not prove that every entry is correctly classified. Equal amounts posted to the wrong accounts can still balance. Review account classification and supporting records where results appear unreasonable.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
8. Income Statement}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The Income Statement summarizes income and expenses for a period. The basic relationship is Income minus Expenses equals Profit or Loss.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Before relying on the report, confirm that income and expense accounts are classified correctly and that the selected accounting period is appropriate.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
9. Balance Sheet}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The Balance Sheet presents the financial position of the business. The basic accounting equation is Assets = Liabilities + Equity.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Cash, bank, petty cash, receivables, equipment and similar resources are generally assets. Payables and loans are generally liabilities. Capital and accumulated results form part of equity according to the accounting structure used.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
10. Petty Cash Module}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The Petty Cash screen includes From, To, Refresh, Generate Monthly Total, and Post Summary to Journal. The Add Petty Cash Entry area visibly includes Date, Description, Account, Type, Receipt, and a Payment field at the right side of the screen.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
A Receipt represents money coming into petty cash. A Payment represents money leaving petty cash. Small expenditures should be assigned to the correct expense account and supported by vouchers or receipts where applicable.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
The screen also contains Monthly Petty Cash Expenses with Expense Head and Amount, followed by a transaction list containing Date, Voucher, Expense Account, Description, Debit, and Credit. The bottom displays Total Debit, Total Credit, Closing Balance, and Monthly Petty Total.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
For the period shown in the supplied Petty Cash screen, the displayed Total Debit is 5,000.00, Total Credit is 1,000.00, and Closing Balance is 4,000.00. Use the detailed entries and expense summary to reconcile the fund before posting.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
11. Monthly Petty Cash Posting}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Use the selected period to review petty cash activity, then Generate Monthly Total and verify the resulting expense information. When satisfied, Post Summary to Journal according to the application workflow.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
Important: do not manually enter the same petty cash expenses in Journal Entries and then post the same summary again. Duplicate posting would overstate expenses and cash movement. After posting, review the Journal, Ledger, and Trial Balance.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
12. Recommended Accounting Workflow}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  1.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
1. Create and review the Chart of Accounts.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  2.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
2. Identify each business transaction and its supporting document.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  3.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
3. Determine the affected accounts.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  4.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
4. Decide the debit and credit treatment.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  5.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
5. Enter the journal voucher and ensure out-of-balance is 0.00.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  6.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
6. Review the relevant ledger accounts.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  7.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
7. Review the Trial Balance.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  8.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
8. Reconcile cash, bank, and petty cash.}
\par \pard\plain \s70\loch\sb0\sa200\contextualspace{\listtext\pard\plain  9.\tab}\ilvl0\ls4 \fi-360\li360\lin360{\loch
9. Review the Income Statement and Balance Sheet.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af7\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f7\fs21\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af11\langfe1033{\loch
10. Investigate unexpected balances before making corrections.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf23\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af9{\loch
